  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1959-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If the legs are \\(a,b\\) and the hypotenuse is \\(c,\\) then \\[ a^2+b^2=c^2=2ab. \\] Hence \\((a-b)^2=0,\\) so the legs are equal. The right triangle is isosceles and its acute angles are \\(45^\\circ.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is C.",
      "hints": [
        "Combine the given relation with the Pythagorean theorem",
        "Compare \\(a^2+b^2\\) with \\(2ab\\)"
      ],
